<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alghu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1266">1266</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alghu was khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a> from 1260 to 1266, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khan">Chagatai Khan</a>. Installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariq-boke">Ariq Böke</a> during the Toluid civil war, he soon turned against him, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> and took control of their revenues. His reign made the Chagatai Khanate a largely independent power rather than a subordinate domain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alghu.jpg" alt="Alghu" width="320" height="547" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miskin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arik_Buka_defeats_Alghu-Rashid_al%27Din_Jami_al_Tavarikhs-large.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
